# Degree of the j-cover of X₁(M) equals [SL₂(ℤ):±Γ₁(M)]

Theorem statement:
`ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqModC_laurentBaseChange_qExpFunctionFieldC_gamma1_eq_index`
(`10bf7192-830c-515d-a576-c2de34f51a07`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `1ed43547-5e10-5194-8d5a-c402bf558c71`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{Q}$, and
let $M$ be a nonzero natural number. Inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ consider the intermediate field $F_0
=$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1
M)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set of all quotients
$\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$ arising from a weight $k$ and two modular forms
$f,g$ for the image of $\Gamma_1(M)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ whose $q$-expansions are given
by integral power series $p_f,p_g$ with $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g \neq 0$. Let $F =$
[`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange K F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) be the intermediate
field of $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by the image of $F_0$ under the coefficientwise embedding
$\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to K((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to K$. Let $y \in F$ be an element whose
underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), namely
$q^{-1}$ times the image in $K$ of the integral power series $E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-\mathrm{unit}}$
(the $q$-expansion of $j$). Then the degree of $F$ over the intermediate field $K(y)$ generated by
$y$ over $K$ is finite and equals the index in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup generated
by $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with $-1$.

This is the classical computation of the degree of the $j$-line cover $X_1(M) \to X(1)$, here in the
form of an equality of field degrees for the $q$-expansion model of the function field of $X_1(M)$
over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero; the upper bound holds for general levels,
and the matching lower bound comes from the tower $K(j) \subseteq K\cdot F(\Gamma_0(M)) \subseteq K
\cdot F(\Gamma_1(M))$ combined with the index identity $[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\pm\Gamma_1(M)] =
\psi(M)\,[(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times : \{\pm 1\}]$. It feeds the later analysis of places and valuations
of this field, including the counting of points in a fibre by double cosets and the descent
arguments for level $N$ structures.

